+<!-- Copyright (c) 2026 Mark Hunter. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later -->
+
+# Backlog Item: _identifier — title_
+
+**Backlog Item ID:** _same identifier as the title_
+
+**Backlog Item Revision:** _revision of this work specification_
+
+Template only. A completed item specifies work; implementation requires a specific
+authorised assignment and acceptance remains governed by HCRL.
+Retain an established item identifier; this template introduces no allocation scheme
+or prescribed revision format. Assignments and evidence reference both header values
+and a source locator that preserves the specific specification used.
+
+## Overview
+
+### High-Level Synopsis of Effort
+
+_Summarise the objective, purpose and bounded effort._
+
+### High-Level Synopsis of Activities
+
+_Summarise the expected work; details belong in Expected / Associated Activity._
+
+### High-Level Synopsis of Outcome
+
+_Summarise the intended observable result._
+
+### High-Level Synopsis of Acceptance Criteria
+
+_Summarise how completion will be judged; details belong in Acceptance Criteria._
+
+## Context
+
+_Explain the current situation, scope, constraints, exclusions and relevant
+architectural/software baseline or source references. Distinguish facts from
+proposals. Use a stable identifier and preserve the referenced item revision._
+
+_Link associated Task Details, Implementation Reports, HCRLs and accepted releases
+as those records become available. An empty future link is not an approval._
+
+## Associated Requirements
+
+_Reference applicable accepted Requirements, Constraints, Goals, Outcomes, Journeys,
+Use Cases, Capabilities, Features or other architectural elements using their
+existing identities/locators and actual standing. Identify proposed changes or
+new elements and their governance dependencies. For justified technical work with
+no applicable requirement, state the rationale; do not manufacture a Motivation
+element or impose a one-to-one mapping._
+
+## Expected / Associated Activity
+
+_Describe the expected work and dependencies sufficiently to bound the assignment.
+Retain engineering autonomy within accepted contracts. Architecture proposals follow
+established governance, ADD and HCRL; this item does not authorise their application._
+
+## Expected Outcomes
+
+_Describe the intended changes, deliverables and observable effects._
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+| Criterion | Observable result | Verification / expected evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| AC-1 | _State a testable or reviewable outcome._ | _Identify how satisfaction will be demonstrated._ |
+
+_Add criteria appropriate to the work. Reference these criteria from evidence
+rather than copying this specification into Tasks, Reports or HCRLs. The common
+solution-wide release verification requirements apply in addition to item criteria._
